  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\n\nThe sfc front will have moved off away from the area Saturday,\nresulting in highs reaching the 70s to low 80s. More chances \nfor storms continue Saturday into Sunday as another mid level \nimpulse and remnant H8 advection persist. Expect PoPs of 50 to \n70%, particularly along and south of Interstate 80 late Saturday\ninto Sunday morning. Rainy conditions continue into Sunday as \nthe closed H5 low now over the northern California coastal area \nfinally treks east into the Northern Plains, providing some lift\nwhile low to mid level moisture transport remains pointed in \nthe area. Rain gradually ends by Monday afternoon as the mid \nlevel wave moves away from the area and sfc high pressure builds\nback in. Mostly dry conditions are progged for Tuesday, while \nour next disturbance approaches for Wednesday and Thursday with \nmore PoPs of 20 to 40% areawide. Temperatures Sunday through at\nleast Wednesday will remain on the cooler side, with highs in \nthe 60s to near 70F. There is some signal for a warm up to the \nupper 70s and low 80s late next week as H5 ridging makes its way\nback toward the area.",
